# The BAKED half of ~/.ssh/config inside dd-dev, copied into the image at
# /home/dev/ssh_config — one of gsrpi-dev-base's seams. At every start the base writes
#
#     $DEV_SECRETS_DIR/ssh_config.fleet    (this repo's identities, if any — on zero,
#                                           ~/.dd-dev-secrets, mounted read-only at
#                                           /run/dd-secrets by infra's dev/compose.yaml)
#     this file                            (the defaults, and nothing else)
#
# into ~/.ssh/config, in that order, because ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each
# keyword. The base also copies every private key in that directory into ~/.ssh at 0600.
#
# NONE OF IT IS NEEDED FOR origin. Since 2026-10-27 git and gh reach
# gsfernandes81/destiny-director over https with the hub's per-repo token, and nothing
# rewrites https to ssh. An ssh identity is only for a remote that token cannot reach —
# e.g. a `github.com-shark` alias for the geolocatingshark remote. Add one on zero, in
# ~/.dd-dev-secrets; nothing in the container can write there.
#
# SO WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR is the defaults, which are all there is when the other half is
# absent (the usual case). It carries NO IdentityFile on purpose: with no identity named,
# an ssh push that has none fails with "Permission denied (publickey)", which is what is
# actually wrong. It matches the base's own copy today; it stays a file of this repo's so
# that what dd-dev's ssh does is decided here, not inherited by accident.

# ── defaults — MUST stay last, and here they are also all there is ──────────
# ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each keyword, so a wildcard above a Host block
# silently wins over it. Anything specific belongs in ssh_config.fleet, which the base
# prepends above this.
Host *
  IdentitiesOnly yes
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 3
